[[Presidential election]]s were scheduled to be held in [[Madagascar]] on 9 November 2023, with a second round on 20 December if required.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2023-09-10 |title=Madagascar president resigns ahead of polls in November |language=en |work=Reuters |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/madagascar-president-resigns-ahead-polls-november-2023-09-10/ |access-date=2023-10-07 |archive-date=2023-10-07 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231007152312/https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/madagascar-president-resigns-ahead-polls-november-2023-09-10/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On 12 October 2023, it was announced that the election would be postponed by one week to 16 November because of pre-election unrest.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2023-09-10 |title=Madagascar court orders one-week postponement of presidential election |language=en |work=Reuters |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/madagascar-court-orders-one-week-postponement-presidential-election-2023-10-12/ |access-date=2023-10-12}}</ref>

[[Andry Rajoelina]] was re-elected to another term with 58.95% of the vote in the first round. Turnout was 46.36%, the lowest in a presidential election in the country's history.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-africa-67517143|title=Andry Rajoelina: Madagascar president re-elected in contested poll|work=BBC News|date=25 November 2023|access-date=26 November 2023}}</ref>

==Electoral system==
The [[President of Madagascar]] is elected using the [[two-round system]]; if no candidate receives a majority of the votes in the first round, a run-off will be held.<ref>[http://www.electionguide.org/elections/id/2293/ Madagascar: Election for President] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220119045924/https://www.electionguide.org/elections/id/2293/ |date=2022-01-19 }} IFES</ref>

==Candidates==
A total of 28 candidates applied to run for the presidency. In the High Constitutional Court decision published on 9 September 2023, only 13 candidates out of 28 were accepted:<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ralison |first=Samuel |date=2023-09-09 |title=Décision n°11-HCC/D3 du 9 septembre 2023 arrêtant la liste définitive des candidats au premier tour de l’élection présidentielle du 9 novembre 2023 |url=http://www.hcc.gov.mg/?p=8484 |access-date=2023-10-07 |language=fr-FR |archive-date=2023-09-11 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230911005013/http://www.hcc.gov.mg/?p=8484 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Election présidentielle à Madagascar : la HCC valide 13 candidatures |url=https://www.linfo.re/ocean-indien/madagascar/election-presidentielle-a-madagascar-la-hcc-valide-13-candidatures |access-date=2023-10-07 |website=Linfo.re |archive-date=2023-09-26 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230926115630/https://www.linfo.re/ocean-indien/madagascar/election-presidentielle-a-madagascar-la-hcc-valide-13-candidatures |url-status=live }}</ref>

They are, by their order on the ballot, decided by [[sortition]]:<ref>{{Cite web |title=Madagascar: Group of candidates for November presidential elections demand rejection of incumbent leader’s bid |url=https://northafricapost.com/70883-madagascar-group-of-candidates-for-november-presidential-elections-demand-rejection-of-incumbent-leaders-bid.html |access-date=2023-10-07 |website=The North Africa Post |language=en-US |archive-date=2023-10-13 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231013060936/https://northafricapost.com/70883-madagascar-group-of-candidates-for-november-presidential-elections-demand-rejection-of-incumbent-leaders-bid.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-09-12 |title=Procès verbal du déroulement du tirage au sort des 13 candidats du lundi 11 Septembre 2023. |url=https://www.ceni-madagascar.mg/proces-verbal-du-deroulement-du-tirage-au-sort-des-13-candidats-du-lundi-11-septembre-2023/ |access-date=2023-10-07 |language=fr-FR |archive-date=2023-10-12 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231012234045/https://www.ceni-madagascar.mg/proces-verbal-du-deroulement-du-tirage-au-sort-des-13-candidats-du-lundi-11-septembre-2023/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

