==Campaign==
During an opposition campaign rally held on 2 October 2023, [[Marc Ravalomanana]], himself a former President and  candidate in the election, suffered a leg injury following the use of teargas by the police.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-10-02 |title=Tear gas fired at opposition in Madagascar |url=https://www.africanews.com/2023/10/02/tear-gas-fired-at-opposition-in-madagascar/ |access-date=2023-10-07 |website=Africanews |language=en |archive-date=2023-10-08 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231008041100/https://www.africanews.com/2023/10/02/tear-gas-fired-at-opposition-in-madagascar/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Rabary |first=Lovasoa |date=2023-10-07 |title=Madagascar presidential candidate injured after opposition rally teargassed |language=en |work=Reuters |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/madagascar-presidential-candidate-shows-injury-after-opposition-rally-teargassed-2023-10-07/ |access-date=2023-10-07 |archive-date=2023-10-07 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231007153308/https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/madagascar-presidential-candidate-shows-injury-after-opposition-rally-teargassed-2023-10-07/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

On the same day, candidate Andry Raobelina suffered an injury to the face from a part of an exploded tear gas canister, which prompted him to call for a report of the election to the Haute cour constitutionnelle. The latter decided on 12 October to move the first round from 9 November to 16 November.<ref>{{cite web|access-date=13 October 2023|date=12 October 2023|title=A Madagascar, l'élection présidentielle est reportée d'une semaine|url=https://information.tv5monde.com/afrique/madagascar-lelection-presidentielle-est-reportee-dune-semaine-2671181|website=TV5MONDE - Informations}}<!-- auto-translated by Module:CS1 translator -->.</ref>

==Conduct==
===Prohibition of political rallies in the open===
In April 2023, incumbent Rajoelina prohibited all political rallies in the open. This was condemned by representatives of the [[European Union]], [[United Kingdom]], [[United States]], [[Germany]], [[France]], [[Switzerland]], [[Norway]] and [[Japan]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=2023-04-06 |title=A Madagascar, le président Andry Rajoelina confine l’opposition |language=fr |work=Le Monde.fr |url=https://www.lemonde.fr/afrique/article/2023/04/06/a-madagascar-le-president-andry-rajoelina-confine-l-opposition_6168516_3212.html |access-date=2023-10-07 |archive-date=2023-10-02 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231002192241/https://www.lemonde.fr/afrique/article/2023/04/06/a-madagascar-le-president-andry-rajoelina-confine-l-opposition_6168516_3212.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Lack of funding ===
In a letter to the [[European Union]] from May 2023 Rajoelina asked for 30 million euros for assisting in organizing the elections.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-05-11 |title=Madagascar: le pays manque d’argent pour organiser l’élection présidentielle |url=https://la1ere.francetvinfo.fr/mayotte/madagascar-le-pays-manque-d-argent-pour-organiser-l-election-presidentielle-1394498.html |access-date=2023-10-07 |website=Mayotte la 1ère |language=fr-FR |archive-date=2023-07-08 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230708182439/https://la1ere.francetvinfo.fr/mayotte/madagascar-le-pays-manque-d-argent-pour-organiser-l-election-presidentielle-1394498.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Dual nationality of Rajoelina===
In June 2023 it was discovered that Rajoelina had acquired French nationality for himself, his wife and their three children in 2014.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2023-06-15 |title=Madagascar: le président Rajoelina est bien français |language=fr |work=Le Monde.fr |url=https://www.lemonde.fr/afrique/article/2023/06/15/madagascar-le-president-rajoelina-est-bien-francais_6177722_3212.html |access-date=2023-10-07 |archive-date=2023-10-02 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231002073516/https://www.lemonde.fr/afrique/article/2023/06/15/madagascar-le-president-rajoelina-est-bien-francais_6177722_3212.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Rabearisoa |first=Sandra |date=2023-06-21 |title=Madagascar: polémique sur la nationalité française du président Andry Rajoelina |url=https://www.aa.com.tr/fr/afrique/madagascar-pol%C3%A9mique-sur-la-nationalit%C3%A9-francaise-du-pr%C3%A9sident-andry-rajoelina/2927834 |access-date=2023-10-07 |website=www.aa.com.tr |language=fr |archive-date=2023-09-04 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230904133529/https://www.aa.com.tr/fr/afrique/madagascar-pol%C3%A9mique-sur-la-nationalit%C3%A9-francaise-du-pr%C3%A9sident-andry-rajoelina/2927834 |url-status=live }}</ref> Under Malagasy law, this may have disqualified him from the presidency, as only citizens of Madagascar are eligible to hold the position, and the country imposes a loss of citizenship if voluntarily acquiring another nationality. Rajoelina argued that he automatically obtained the French nationality through his father and only formalized it, meaning he had not voluntarily switched. The Constitutional Court eventually sided with him, pointing out the lack of a decree officially removing his Malagasy nationality.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-11-16 |title=Low turnout in boycott-hit Madagascar presidential election |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20231116-low-turnout-in-boycott-hit-madagascar-presidential-election |access-date=2023-11-20 |website=France 24 |language=en}}</ref>

===Case of Romy Voos Andrianarisoa===
On 14 August 2023 the Director of Cabinet of President Andry Rajoelina, Romy Voos Andrianarisoa, was arrested in [[London]] under accusations of corruption in a London-based mining company.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-08-14 |title=Suspicion De Corruption - Romy Andrianarisoa arrêtée au Royaume-Uni |url=https://lexpress.mg/14/08/2023/suspicion-de-corruption-romy-andrianarisoa-arretee-au-royaume-uni/ |access-date=2023-10-07 |website=L'Express de Madagascar |language=fr-FR |archive-date=2023-08-16 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230816051030/https://lexpress.mg/14/08/2023/suspicion-de-corruption-romy-andrianarisoa-arretee-au-royaume-uni/ |url-status=live }}</ref> She was then dismissed by Rajoelina on 16 August.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-08-16 |title=Tentative de corruption : En détention provisoire à Londres, la Dircab de la Présidence, limogée |url=https://midi-madagasikara.mg/tentative-de-corruption-en-detention-provisoire-a-londres-la-dircab-de-la-presidence-limogee/ |access-date=2023-10-07 |website=Midi Madagasikara |language=fr-FR |archive-date=2023-08-16 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230816051038/https://midi-madagasikara.mg/tentative-de-corruption-en-detention-provisoire-a-londres-la-dircab-de-la-presidence-limogee/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On a rally of the opposition in Antananarivo on November 13, [[Paraina August]], one of the ten protester candidates and former speaker of the lower house of the Malagasy parliament, claimed that London would have emitted a summons letter to one of the running candidates without specifically mentioning a name. This claim was interpreted by the police as a public defamation, spread of fake news, and incitement to hatred. A few hours later, Paraina August was arrested at the international airport of Ivato and detained by the police for a couple of hours before finally being released.<ref>{{cite web |work=Midi Madagascar |date = 2023-11-15|title=Paraina Auguste:Le candidat arrêté et auditionné auprès de la cybercriminalité|url=https://midi-madagasikara.mg/paraina-auguste-le-candidat-arrete-et-auditionne-aupres-de-la-cybercriminalite/|access-date=2023-11-15 }} </ref>

===Prohibition of an opposition meeting===
On 5 September 2023 a meeting of the candidates of the opposition was prevented by the police.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-09-05 |title=Les candidats de l’opposition empêchés de se réunir |url=https://midi-madagasikara.mg/les-candidats-de-lopposition-empeches-de-se-reunir/ |access-date=2023-10-07 |website=Midi Madagasikara |language=fr-FR |archive-date=2023-09-14 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230914051926/https://midi-madagasikara.mg/les-candidats-de-lopposition-empeches-de-se-reunir/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

===Opposition boycott===
The political opposition largely boycotted the elections.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Voting ends in Madagascar presidential election boycotted by opposition |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/16/madagascar-kicks-off-presidential-polls-amid-calls-for-boycott |access-date=2023-11-20 |website=Al Jazeera |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2023-11-16 |title=Madagascar polls close and opposition shuns votes |language=en-GB |work=BBC News |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-africa-67426287 |access-date=2023-11-20}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Eligon |first=John |date=2023-11-16 |title=Madagascar Votes Amid Violence and Calls for Boycott |language=en-US |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/16/world/africa/madagascar-vote-violence-boycott.html |access-date=2023-11-20 |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

